{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Root cause found 2026-11-16 (PST 11:05-12:15)\n\nStatus of related tickets: short-elderly-cock (reconnect window) and teenage-unquieted-ringworm (parallel-call OOM) are both closed `preexisting`; neither changed allocator behaviour, and the plateau reproduces on deployed `b4e0d01b649`.\n\n**Live (read-only SSM), `rebar-mcp-b4e0d01b6491-8092`:** idle at 342 MB 15:38-18:55 UTC; plan-review jobs 19:01-19:44 UTC; then 6 samples 19:47-20:11 UTC all `anon=1273MB`, `RssAnon=1273MB`, 4 threads, 0 calls. PID 1 is the only process. smaps: 703 MB in 11 glibc thread-arena heaps, 547 MB other anon, 22 MB `[heap]`. cgroup `memory.peak` since start 3.04 GB, `oom 0`.\n\n**Local, MCP base image (`python:3.12-slim`), isolated store clone, no model credentials:**\n- 6 concurrent store reads: peak 656 MB, idle 71 MB (released).\n- Gate-shaped synthetic worker thread (~1 GB of large strings dropped, 1,200 small survivors): idle RssAnon 983 MB, `mallinfo2` free 970 MB; `malloc_trim(0)` -> 24 MB in 70 ms. Reproduces the hold.\n- `verify_completion` x2 with a stubbed `TestModel` (no Bedrock): 65 -> 115 -> 127 MB; trim -> 119 MB. The stub path allocates little, so it does not reproduce the full gate footprint; the live model turn's prompts/tool output are the large allocations.\n- Separate small growth seen: ~115k Python blocks per gate run (botocore service-model `OrderedDict`s, ~18k per run). Not the plateau (tens of MB, not GB); not addressed here.\n\n**Fix:** `malloc_trim(0)` when the in-flight gauge returns to zero (commit `dd483029d2d`, pending review). New test fails without it (\"idle process kept 252 MiB\") and passes with it, on Linux.\n\n**Unverified until deploy:** what share of the live 1,273 MB is free-but-held (trimmable) versus live objects; the post-deploy AC records it."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1794860082587854924,"uuid":"9eeb9042-dfc3-483b-af81-af243bac4008"}